From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:41:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 082/106] ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice: arm the call taps the way the
 vendor does

When the taps are armed as part of starting a call, do it in the vendor
order - in-call playback first, then recording - and only tap the
directions record_dirs asks for. Tapping the uplink hands the microphone
to the record port instead of copying it, so the far end hears nothing
at all; the default is now the downlink alone.

Arming both directions unconditionally is what made incall_taps unusable
before.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
index 8fcf7c40b..0aa77d325 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
@@ -319,14 +319,28 @@ static int q6voice_path_start(struct q6voice_path *p)
 	 * call that is otherwise working.
 	 */
 	if (incall_taps) {
-		ret = q6cvs_start_record(p->runtime->sessions[Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVS],
-					 true, true);
+		struct q6voice_session *cvs =
+			p->runtime->sessions[Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVS];
+
+		/*
+		 * Playback before recording, the order the vendor driver uses
+		 * when it brings these up as part of starting a call.
+		 */
+		ret = q6cvs_start_playback(cvs);
 		if (ret)
-			dev_dbg(dev, "in-call record taps not started: %d\n", ret);
+			dev_dbg(dev, "in-call playback not started: %d\n", ret);
 
-		ret = q6cvs_start_playback(p->runtime->sessions[Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVS]);
+		/*
+		 * Which directions to tap comes from record_dirs (1 = the far
+		 * end, 2 = the microphone, 3 = both). Tapping the microphone
+		 * takes it away from the modem instead of copying it, so the
+		 * default is the far end alone.
+		 */
+		if (record_dirs)
+			ret = q6cvs_start_record(cvs, record_dirs & 1,
+						 record_dirs & 2);
 		if (ret)
-			dev_dbg(dev, "in-call playback not started: %d\n", ret);
+			dev_dbg(dev, "in-call record taps not started: %d\n", ret);
 		ret = 0;
 	}
 
